    "title": "Cam Young's net worth and very private wife who encouraged 'new look'",
    "text": "Cameron Young is supported by his wife Kelsey Dalition at the Masters -Credit:Andrew Redington/Getty Images (Andrew Redington/Getty Images)Cameron Young enters the final round of the Masters leading alongside Rory McIlroy - and with his family supporting him every step of the way.Young enjoyed a breakthrough PGA Tour season last year, earning a Ryder Cup call-up, then has carried that momentum into 2026. He recently won The Players Championship, where he was asked an awkward question about not smiling in the aftermath.Young is now eyeing his first major win and a massive career milestone. He's playing the final round alongside Rory McIlroy, who aimed a thinly-veiled dig at his playing partner.Off the course, Young's journey is defined by both financial achievement and the understated yet significant support of his wife, Kelsey Dalition, who has even shaped the way he carries himself on golf's grandest stages.• Phil Mickelson behavior toward Masters locker room staff in parking lot after win said it all• Masters security crackdown launched as influencers threaten strict ruleWhat is Cameron Young's Net WorthAs of 2025, Cameron Young's net worth is estimated to be roughly $17 to $18 million.This amount reflects his recent breakthrough, including his maiden PGA Tour victory at the Wyndham Championship in early August 2025, where he dominated the competition and claimed a substantial winner's check of nearly $1.5 million, then landed $4.5 million for winning this year's Players Championship.Young celebrated with his family after winning The Players Championship -Credit:David Cannon/Getty ImagesBeyond his tournament winnings, his career prize money, including majors, is $38 million according to Spotrac.He also benefits from multiple endorsement partnerships - having represented brands such as Peter Millar and iCapital, among others - which significantly supplement his income away from the course.Who is Cameron Young's Wife?Young is married to Kelsey Dalition, a notably private individual who rarely features on social media and chooses to maintain her personal life away from public scrutiny. The pair wed in an intimate ceremony in 2021, just after Young turned professional, with his former college teammate and caddie, Scott McKean, serving as best man.Kelsey holds qualifications as a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) and competed in collegiate golf at Wake Forest University. Despite maintaining a low public profile, she consistently attends his tournaments in a supportive capacity, including The Masters Par‐3 Contest and the 2025 Genesis Invitational, frequently accompanied by their children.An individual dressed in a white polo shirt and a white cap is addressing the press at a podium, with a microphone positioned in front of him. The backdrop features a combination of logos and text, creating a visually distinct and professional setting for the media engagement.The family calls Jupiter, Florida home, having bought property there in 2022 following an earlier period living with Young's parents. The couple have three children together, including their firstborn, Henry, who arrived in 2022.Young's 'new look'One revealing episode that highlighted Kelsey Dalition's quiet influence came prior to the 2023 PGA Championship at Oak Hill Country Club. Recognized for his distinctive facial hair, Cameron showed up to the tournament clean-shaven, an unexpected transformation he attributed to his wife's recommendation.As he put it, \"Honestly, my wife just kind of said, why don't you shave... I haven't been clean‐shaven probably since our first son was born.\"",
